            <h3 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold text-stone-900 leading-tight">Do you repair broken garage door springs?</h3>
          </div>
          
          <div class="prose prose-stone max-w-none mb-8">
            <p class="text-stone-600 leading-relaxed font-semibold mb-4 text-lg text-red-600">Yes! But please, never attempt to replace or adjust a garage door spring yourself.</p>
            <p class="text-stone-600 leading-relaxed mb-4">Garage door torsion and extension springs are under extreme, life-threatening tension. When a spring snaps, it sounds like a gunshot, and the door will immediately become too heavy for the opener to lift. Trying to bypass the motor or replace the spring without the proper winding bars and training can result in severe injury.</p>
            <p class="text-stone-600 leading-relaxed mb-4"><strong>What you need to know about our spring repair:</strong></p>
            <ul class="space-y-2 text-stone-600 mb-4 list-disc pl-5">
              <li><strong>Lifespan:</strong> A standard builder-grade spring lasts about 10,000 cycles (roughly 5-7 years for an average family). We offer high-cycle replacements that last significantly longer.</li>
              <li><strong>Replace in Pairs:</strong> If your door has two springs and one breaks, the other is right at the end of its lifespan. We always replace both to ensure perfectly balanced tension.</li>
              <li><strong>Weight Calibration:</strong> We carry a massive inventory of springs on our trucks to precisely match the weight of your specific door on the very first visit.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          
          <div class="bg-stone-50 border border-stone-200 p-6 rounded-xl flex flex-col sm:flex-row justify-between items-center gap-6">
            <p class="text-stone-800 font-semibold text-center sm:text-left">Trapped in your garage?</p>
            <a href="tel:+10000000000" class="w-full sm:w-auto text-center bg-stone-900 text-white font-bold py-3 px-8 rounded-lg shadow-md hover:bg-black transition-colors">Call For Emergency Service</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </dialog>

